  "raw_meta_yaml": "{% set name = \"argon2-cffi-bindings\" %}\n{% set version = \"26.1.0\" %}\n\npackage:\n  name: {{ name|lower }}\n  version: {{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/{{ name[0] }}/{{ name }}/{{ name | replace('-', '_') }}-{{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: \"63505c71542a44b68b1e38060450fb006404170da375feb31af153e7f9c6205d\"\n\nbuild:\n  number: 1\n  script_env:\n    - ARGON2_CFFI_USE_SSE2=0  # [not x86_64]\n  script:\n    - ln -sf $RANLIB $BUILD_PREFIX/bin/ranlib  # [unix]\n    # Without this CMake falls back to \"Unix Makefiles\" and there is no make\n    # in the build env, so configuration fails before a compiler is probed.\n    - export CMAKE_GENERATOR=Ninja  # [unix]\n    # FindPython has to run the interpreter to locate headers, which CMP0190\n    # forbids while cross-compiling. Upstream's cmake_minimum_required\n    # (3.20...4.3) raises the policy max past 4.1, so the policy is NEW here\n    # and every cross target fails to find Python. conda's cross-python ships\n    # a native shim that answers for the target, so running it is safe.\n    - export CMAKE_ARGS=\"${CMAKE_ARGS} -DCMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR=/usr/bin/env\"  # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - {{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - python                                 # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - cross-python_{{ target_platform }}     # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - {{ compiler(\"c\") }}\n    - {{ stdlib(\"c\") }}\n    - cmake\n    - ninja\n\n  host:\n    - python\n    - pip\n    - scikit-build-core >=1.0\n    - setuptools_scm >=8\n\n  run:\n    - python\n    - cffi >=1.0.1                           # [py < 314]\n    - cffi >=2.0.0b1                         # [py >= 314]\n\ntest:\n  files:\n    - test_bindings.py\n    - test_win_arm64.py  # [win and arm64]\n  imports:\n    - _argon2_cffi_bindings\n  requires:\n    - pip\n  commands:\n    - python test_bindings.py\n    - python test_win_arm64.py  # [win and arm64]\n    - pip check\n\nabout:\n  home: https://github.com/hynek/argon2-cffi-bindings\n  license: MIT\n  license_family: MIT\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  summary: Low-level Python CFFI Bindings for Argon2\n  description: |\n    argon2-cffi-bindings provides low-level CFFI bindings to the Argon2\n    password hashing algorithm including a vendored version of them.\n  doc_url: https://github.com/hynek/argon2-cffi-bindings\n  dev_url: https://github.com/hynek/argon2-cffi-bindings\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - stuertz\n",
